{"tool_name":"ghostz","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"ghostz","version":"1.0.2","home":"http://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/ghostz","documentation":"http://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/ghostz","license":"BSD-2-Clause","summary":"GHOSTZ is a highly efficient remote homologue detection tool.","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btu780","biotools:ghostz"],"description":"GHOSTZ is a homology search tool which can detect remote homologues like BLAST and is about 200 times more efficient than BLAST by using database subsequence clustering. GHOSTZ outputs search results in the format similar to BLAST-tabular format.","license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"number":7,"run_exports":[null],"skip":true},"requirements":{"build":["make",null,null],"host":["libgomp","llvm-openmp"],"run":["libgomp","llvm-openmp"]},"source_url":"http://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/ghostz/releases/ghostz-1.0.2.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["ghostz -h | grep \"homology search tool\""]},"recipe_maintainers":["tomkinsc"]},"biocontainers":{"name":"ghostz","identifiers":["biotools:ghostz","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btu780"],"license":"BSD-2-Clause","summary":"GHOSTZ is a highly efficient remote homologue detection tool","home_url":"http://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/ghostz/","keywords":["Amino Acid Sequence","Animals","Cluster Analysis","Databases, Genetic","Humans","Metagenomics","Military Personnel","Molecular Sequence Data","Programming Languages","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Sequence Homology","Soil","DNA","Sequence analysis","Molecular genetics","Clustering","Protein Sequences"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"ghostz","home":"http://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/ghostz/","summary":"Homology search tool which can detect remote homologues like BLAST and is about 200 times more efficient than BLAST by using database subsequence clustering. GHOSTZ outputs search results in the format similar to BLAST-tabular format.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:44:18Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:18:12.541600Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["BLAST"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:ghostz","credit":[{"email":"akiyama@cs.titech.ac.jp","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/ghostz/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Homology-based gene prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3663"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence search results","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0857"}}]}],"name":"GHOSTZ","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btu780","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Sequence homology searches are used in various fields. New sequencing technologies produce huge amounts of sequence data, which continuously increase the size of sequence databases. As a result, homology searches require large amounts of computational time, especially for metagenomic analysis. Results: We developed a fast homology search method based on database subsequence clustering, and implemented it as GHOSTZ. This method clusters similar subsequences from a database to perform an efficient seed search and ungapped extension by reducing alignment candidates based on triangle inequality. The database subsequence clustering technique achieved an \u00e2 1/42-fold increase in speed without a large decrease in search sensitivity. When we measured with metagenomic data, GHOSTZ is \u00e2 1/42.2-2.8 times faster than RAPSearch and is \u00e2 1/4185-261 times faster than BLASTX. Availability and implementation: The source code is freely available for download at http://www.bi.cs.titech.ac.jp/ghostz/.","authors":[{"name":"Akiyama Y."},{"name":"Ishida T."},{"name":"Kakuta M."},{"name":"Suzuki S."}],"citationCount":34,"date":"2015-04-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Faster sequence homology searche